WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.400
Can we make our coffee taste better by brewing the same grounds twice?

2
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:08.280
You see this a lot with tea where it's re-steeped, but we want to try it with coffee. Using the Harrier switch

3
00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:11.680
We're going to do a traditional pour over. We're using 15 grams of coffee and to that

4
00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:15.960
We're going to add 240 grams of water. We're going to start with the classic bloom. 50 grams

5
00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:18.760
And we're going to leave that for 30 seconds and at the 30 second mark

6
00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:22.280
We're going to top that up to 240 grams. Now we're going to close this switch

7
00:00:22.280 --> 00:00:26.800
This will allow us to do an immersion for the second brew, but we're not using water for the second grounds

8
00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:28.520
We're going to pour the coffee back through the bed

9
00:00:28.520 --> 00:00:31.720
Then we're going to steep that for 30 seconds at the 30 second mark

10
00:00:31.720 --> 00:00:35.120
We're going to open the switch and allow that to drain. Is it better now?

11
00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:37.120
We'll taste just the regular filter coffee

12
00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:41.440
It's nice clean black current and now we'll taste the double brewed coffee

13
00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:45.040
You're probably getting a few negative characteristics coming through from that second brew

14
00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:48.600
But there is a lot more sweetness if you value body and sweetness

15
00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:51.760
This is a really good way to increase that in your coffee coffee undecided

